{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794063972,"nonce":"V0Ja/21xtOr8/ylw4JyG0GMAEKY=","message":"Weak tables, ephemerons and finalizers now work under ZYNTAX_HOST_HEAP=immix. The Lua conformance suite passes 46 of 46 with Immix selected, and the pool path still passes its gc cases.\n\nA collection runs the registered WeakHooks (hold before the roots, trace and settle after marking drains), then the weak sweepers, then the sweep. After-collection callbacks, where finalizers run, run once the heap locks are released.\n\nThree things the first pass missed, each of which kept a dead value alive or misreported the heap:\n- Stack ranges hidden with hide_stack were still scanned. They are filtered the same way as in the pool collector.\n- The register spill happens in collector::collect itself, so no wrapper frame sits between the spill and the caller.\n- collectgarbage(\"count\") lagged because open bump regions are charged only when retired. Stats now add the calling thread's open regions.\n\nStill open: pointer-free allocation hint, inline bump for compiled code, prefetch in the mark loop, returning memory to the OS, parallel mark, line-level evacuation, multi-thread stop-the-world. The speed gap against the pool collector is unchanged by this work and was not re-measured.","files":null}]}